\f0\fs22\cf1
\pard\sb240\sa60\b\fs32 iPad → DEVONthink: Multi-Page Document Capture\b0\par
\par
\pard Four methods depending on what you are capturing and where you are in the workflow.\par
\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdr0\par
\par
\pard\sb200\sa60\b\fs28 Method 1 – Safari web pages (easiest, no extra tools)\b0\par
\par
\pard\li360\fi-360 Open the page in Safari.\par
\pard\li360\fi-360 Take a screenshot (Side button + Volume Up).\par
\pard\li360\fi-360 Tap the \b preview thumbnail\b0 in the bottom-left corner.\par
\pard\li360\fi-360 Tap \b "Full Page"\b0 at the top of the editor.\par
\pard    - Safari renders the entire page as a single tall PDF automatically.\par
\pard\li360\fi-360 Tap the \b Share\b0 button → \b DEVONthink To Go\b0 → choose your group → \b Import\b0.\par
\par
\pard This works for any website and requires nothing extra.\par
\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdr0\par
\par
\pard\sb200\sa60\b\fs28 Method 2 – Markup screenshot direct to a DTTG group (recommended for New Scientist etc.)\b0\par
\par
\pard This method replaces the cumbersome route of Markup → Save to Files → navigate to Files → share to DTTG. Instead, you share directly from inside Markup and the file lands in the correct DTTG group in one step.\par
\par
\pard\sb160\sa40\b\fs24 How it works\b0\par
\par
\pard DEVONthink To Go provides its own \b Shortcuts actions\b0, including "Create Item in DEVONthink To Go", which can receive a file and place it into a named database and group — no DTTG interface interaction required. A Shortcut placed in the iOS Share Sheet becomes available as a one-tap action from anywhere: Markup, Files, Photos, Safari, or any other app.\par
\par
\pard\sb160\sa40\b\fs24 One-time setup: create the Shortcut\b0\par
\par
\pard Open the \b Shortcuts\b0 app on your iPad and create a new Shortcut named \b "File to DTTG"\b0.\par
\par
\b Step  |  Action  |  Setting\b0\par
\b 1  |  **Receive** input  |  Type: Any · From: Share Sheet and Shortcuts\b0\par
\b 2  |  **Choose from Menu**  |  Prompt: "File to which group?"\b0\par
\b 3  |  ↳ Menu item: **"New Scientist"**  |  —\b0\par
\b 4  |  ↳↳ **Create Item in DEVONthink To Go**  |  Item: Shortcut Input · Database: (your database) · Group: New Scientist\b0\par
\b 5  |  ↳ Menu item: **"Fire Defence"**  |  —\b0\par
\b 6  |  ↳↳ **Create Item in DEVONthink To Go**  |  Item: Shortcut Input · Database: (your database) · Group: Fire Defence\b0\par
\b 7  |  ↳ Menu item: **"Inbox"**  |  —\b0\par
\b 8  |  ↳↳ **Create Item in DEVONthink To Go**  |  Item: Shortcut Input · Database: (your database) · Group: Inbox\b0\par
\par
\pard Add or remove menu items to match your actual DTTG groups. The "Create Item in DEVONthink To Go" action is found by searching \b "DEVONthink"\b0 in the Shortcuts action library — it only appears after DTTG is installed.\par
\par
\pard\sb160\sa40\b\fs24 Using it from Markup\b0\par
\par
\pard\li360\fi-360 Take a screenshot (Side button + Volume Up) — or open an existing image in Markup.\par
\pard\li360\fi-360 Annotate as needed in Markup.\par
\pard\li360\fi-360 Tap the \b Share button\b0 (arrow-out-of-box, top right) — \b not\b0 Done → Save to Files.\par
\pard\li360\fi-360 In the share sheet, tap \b "File to DTTG"\b0 (your Shortcut).\par
\pard\li360\fi-360 Tap the group name you want.\par
\pard\li360\fi-360 The file appears in that DTTG group immediately. Syncs to DEVONthink on your Mac via the Contabo syncstore.\par
\par
\pard\sb160\sa40\b\fs24 Using it from Files (for files already saved there)\b0\par
\par
\pard\li360\fi-360 Open \b Files\b0, navigate to the saved file.\par
\pard\li360\fi-360 Long-press the file → \b Share\b0.\par
\pard\li360\fi-360 Tap \b "File to DTTG"\b0 in the share sheet.\par
\pard\li360\fi-360 Choose the group.\par
\par
\pard\sb160\sa40\b\fs24 Notes\b0\par
\par
\pard\li360\fi-360\bullet  The Shortcut works for any file type: PNG, JPG, PDF, even text files.\par
\pard\li360\fi-360\bullet  If "Create Item in DEVONthink To Go" does not appear in the Shortcuts action library, check that DTTG is installed and open Settings → DEVONthink To Go → allow Siri & Shortcuts.\par
\pard\li360\fi-360\bullet  The file goes straight into the group — DTTG does not need to be open or in the foreground.\par
\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdr0\par
\par
\pard\sb200\sa60\b\fs28 Method 3 – iOS Shortcut for multi-page scrolling documents\b0\par
\par
\pard Use this when the document is longer than one screen in an app that does not support Full Page export (not Safari).\par
\par
\pard\sb160\sa40\b\fs24 Shortcut steps\b0\par
\par
\b Step  |  Action  |  Setting\b0\par
\b 1  |  **Ask for Input**  |  Prompt: "Document title?" · Input type: Text\b0\par
\b 2  |  Set variable  |  **doc_title** ← Shortcut Input\b0\par
\b 3  |  **Repeat**  |  (loop indefinitely)\b0\par
\b 4  |  ↳ Take Screenshot  |  —\b0\par
\b 5  |  ↳ Add to Variable  |  Variable: **screenshots**\b0\par
\b 6  |  ↳ **Choose from Menu**  |  Prompt: "More pages?" · Options: "Yes, scroll & continue" / "No, done"\b0\par
\b 7  |  ↳ If "No, done" → **Exit Repeat**  |  —\b0\par
\b 8  |  **Combine Images**  |  Images: **screenshots** · Layout: Vertically\b0\par
\b 9  |  **Make PDF**  |  Input: combined image · Page size: actual size\b0\par
\b 10  |  **Choose from Menu**  |  Prompt: "File to which group?" (same group menu as Method 2)\b0\par
\b 11  |  ↳ **Create Item in DEVONthink To Go**  |  Item: PDF from step 9 · Group: chosen group\b0\par
\par
\pard\sb160\sa40\b\fs24 How to use it\b0\par
\par
\pard\li360\fi-360 Navigate to the first screen of the document.\par
\pard\li360\fi-360 Run the Shortcut from your Home Screen or the Shortcuts widget.\par
\pard\li360\fi-360 Enter a title.\par
\pard\li360\fi-360 Take screenshot, scroll, tap \b "Yes"\b0, repeat for each screen.\par
\pard\li360\fi-360 On the last screen tap \b "No, done"\b0.\par
\pard\li360\fi-360 Choose the DTTG group — the stitched PDF is filed immediately.\par
\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdr0\par
\par
\pard\sb200\sa60\b\fs28 Method 4 – Automatic Mac-side stitching (best image quality, optional)\b0\par
\par
\pard Use this only when you need the overlap-trimming that the iOS Shortcut cannot provide — for example, very long documents where duplicate scroll regions are visible in the stitched result.\par
\par
\pard\sb160\sa40\b\fs24 Setup (one time, on your Mac)\b0\par
\par
\f1\fs18\cf2
pip3 install Pillow numpy watchdog\line
\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\par
\pard\sb160\sa40\b\fs24 Watch mode\b0\par
\par
\f1\fs18\cf2
python3 watch_and_import.py \\\line
    ~/Library/Mobile\\ Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/Screenshots \\\line
    --group "Fire Defence"\line
\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\par
\pard Screenshots synced via iCloud are automatically stitched, trimmed, and imported into DEVONthink on the Mac. DEVONthink then syncs the result back to DTTG via the Contabo syncstore.\par
\par
\pard\sb160\sa40\b\fs24 One-off manual stitch\b0\par
\par
\f1\fs18\cf2
python3 stitch_to_devonthink.py page1.png page2.png page3.png \\\line
    --import --group "Fire Defence"\line
\f0\fs22\cf1\par
\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdr0\par
\par
\pard\sb200\sa60\b\fs28 Choosing the right method\b0\par
\par
\b Situation  |  Method\b0\par
\b Web page in Safari  |  1 – Full Page screenshot\b0\par
\b Markup screenshot or any single-page file  |  2 – "File to DTTG" Shortcut via Share button\b0\par
\b File already saved in the Files app  |  2 – same Shortcut, from Files share sheet\b0\par
\b Multi-page scrolling document, any app  |  3 – screenshot loop Shortcut\b0\par
\b Very long document, overlap trimming needed  |  4 – Mac script\b0\par
